{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"86372cbd4b76439edb9041576abb7dfc01d63bf176d0f30946645635dc750c60","digest":{"component_or_area":"bridge suggest-mapping command","key_entities":["rebar bridge suggest-mapping","mapping_probe.py","mapping_config.py","_bridge_suggest_mapping","_emit_nested_toml","_emit_config_toml","src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/bridge.py","src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/mapping_probe.py","jira.JIRA.issue_types()","jira.JIRA.priorities()","jira.JIRA.issue_link_types()","jira.JIRA.statuses()","jira.JIRA.createmeta_issuetypes()","jira.JIRA.search_issues()","jira.JIRA.transitions()","[tool.rebar.mapping]","rebar.toml","issue_types","statuses","link_types","priority_map","status_map","hierarchy","create_defaults"],"problem_keywords":["mapping configuration","jira probe","suggest-mapping command","vocabulary discovery","axis mapping","toml serialization","read-only probe"],"propositions":["A new read-only command `rebar bridge suggest-mapping <PROJECT>` probes a live Jira instance via pycontribs to discover vocabulary (issue types, statuses, link types, priorities) and emits a pre-populated `[tool.rebar.mapping]` block.","The probe uses only documented public pycontribs methods (issue_types, priorities, issue_link_types, statuses, createmeta APIs, search_issues, transitions) and never makes private REST calls or writes to Jira.","The `--write` flag atomically merges the suggested mapping block into an existing rebar.toml or creates one, preserving pre-existing flat sections and hand-edited mapping keys (existing keys win), never modifying pyproject.toml.","Transition hints are marked best-effort/partial because they are grounded only in sample issues' current-status transitions, not a complete state graph.","Two new nested TOML emission helpers (`_emit_nested_toml` and `_emit_config_toml`) handle the mixed flat/nested structure of rebar.toml while preserving the existing fail-closed `_emit_toml` contract.","The probe port architecture supports offline unit testing via fake ports returning canned data, with no live Jira credentials or CI gating required."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787427900173322001,"uuid":"18c70158-004b-435d-8418-fda39f0d35eb"}